    directAnswer: "A modern seaport combines deep-water berths and wharf structures with container yards, crane rails, intermodal connections, and gate complexes. Engineering covers dredging and marine structures, heavy-duty pavements for container stacking, deep crane-rail foundations, stormwater for vast paved areas, high-mast lighting, reefer electrical systems, and truck gate throughput.",
