    directAnswer: "A transit bus garage is a long-span indoor facility for fleet parking, maintenance, and dispatch. Engineering covers clear-span structures for bus maneuvering, floor slabs for bus axle loads, ventilation and gas detection for indoor vehicle storage, CNG or electric fueling infrastructure, fire protection for fuel-loaded vehicles, and maintenance bay equipment.",
